name: blank-project-behind-home-inherited
description: "The blank project behind Home is inherited and can't be removed cheaply; Kenneth's rule from 2026-11-02: save only when a model is present or the project was already saved"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: 652e487a-cf34-4bb4-8055-6939f0667d89
  modified: 2026-11-02T18:27:34.325Z
---

The blank project behind Home was never designed or approved. OrcaSlicer's Plater holds `Slic3r::Model model` as a value member and calls `new_project` at startup (upstream `EVT_RESTORE_PROJECT` handler). JusPrin's shell keeps that Plater and gives the empty project an identity (`ProjectPersistence::attach`, `ProjectAutosave`). The "untouched startup draft" existed from 076ed1d4c3 (2026-09-30).

9d565b8e6b (2026-10-28) removed the startup reopen that used to replace the draft, so the draft became what stays open. Kenneth's words on 2026-10-28 covered only the reopen: "Let's assume this is a bug." An agent told them the removal meant "starting on Home with nothing open", and an agent brief added "a blank draft behind it".

On 2026-11-02 Kenneth's rule: "Save when a model is present, the project was already saved, or a chat has messages. drop chats." So two conditions: `blank()` in `ProjectAutosave.cpp`. They accepted that chats on an empty plate are lost on restart or when a file is opened. A first version with a list of what counts as work (`holds_work`) was replaced the same day; check the rule landed before relying on it.

Open question: nobody decided whether the app should tell the person a chat on an empty plate won't be kept; the header still reads as saved.

**Why:** On 2026-11-02 Kenneth remembered a commit forbidding a project at launch; that commit forbids only a saved one.

**How to apply:** Don't call the blank project intended, or 9d565b8e6b its origin. Don't add a third save condition without asking. See [[trace-a-rule-to-kenneths-words]] and [[autosave-design-research]].
bool ProjectAutosave::save_now()
{
    try {
        adopt_project();
        settle(true); // A failed older write can be retried from the live model.
        m_store->ensure_durable_head();
        observe_document_change();
        if (blank()) {
            m_error.clear();
            m_state = State::Saved;
            return true;
        }
        if (!m_store->head_id().empty() && !m_last_capture_input.empty() &&
            observed_input() == m_last_capture_input) {
            if (m_persistence.document().doc_revision() != m_committed_semantic_revision)
                return persist_document(true);
            m_error.clear();
            m_state = State::Saved;
            return true;
        }
        GLCanvas3D* canvas = m_plater.get_view3D_canvas3D();
        if (canvas == nullptr || !canvas->is_initialized()) {
            fail("The project canvas is not ready for a durable save");
            return false;
        }
        if (canvas->get_gizmos_manager().is_in_editing_mode(true)) {
            fail("Finish the current tool edit before replacing the project");
            return false;
        }
        return capture(true);
    } catch (const std::exception& error) {
        fail(error.what());
        return false;
    }
}

